# Third-party notices

Third-party code, weights and data retain their original licenses. The project's
integration license does not relicense them. Exact source snapshots are listed
in `UPSTREAM.json`; models are downloaded to ignored local storage, with fixed
URLs, lengths and SHA256 checks in `resources/models.json`.

## V3 implementation and resources

- [MOPELotus/Lotus-ReFactor](https://github.com/MOPELotus/Lotus-ReFactor): V3 wire
  protocol, preprocessing, original five-model recognition and external provider
  clients were ported to TypeScript at the copyright owner's request. Original
  terms: `licenses/Lotus-ReFactor-LICENSE`.
- [Pillow](https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow): RGB resize semantics in
  `src/infrastructure/resize.ts`; original notice retained at
  `resources/captcha/Pillow-LICENSE.txt`.
- [luguoyixiazi/test_nine](https://github.com/luguoyixiazi/test_nine) and
  [luguoyixiazi/model_save](https://huggingface.co/luguoyixiazi/model_save):
  original inference reference and unchanged V3 HGNet, D-FINE, YOLO, DINO and
  attention weights. The model repository API declares no model-card license;
  no blanket MIT grant is inferred. Weight files are not committed to Git.

## wulu GeeTest V4 ports

[wulu007/geetest-bypass](https://github.com/wulu007/geetest-bypass) is MIT;
original copyright/license is preserved in `third_party/wulu-geetest-bypass/LICENSE`.
The protocol, PoW, encryption, track, image and voice implementations have been
ported/adapted into their corresponding TypeScript modules. Original third-party
notices and each extension's LICENSE/NOTICE are retained under that directory.
The original Python programs are not part of the runtime distribution.

Voice NPZ arrays were losslessly serialized into JSON. This is a format change,
not training or modification of learned values. Phrase OCR character data was
extracted from the model already used by RapidOCR; its license remains applicable.

The original notices distinguish GeekedTest icon material (MIT), PP-OCRv6
(Apache-2.0), LibreYOLO9t-derived character detection (MIT), and UER Chinese
RoBERTa derivatives (base model card declares no license). Preserve those
individual declarations rather than applying the HuggingFace repository's
Apache-2.0 card to every underlying resource.

Inspection of the actual downloaded **icon-direction** and old **phrase-detect**
files additionally reveals **AGPL-3.0 model metadata**. That metadata is retained
in `resources/model-metadata.json`; these weights are not relabeled MIT here.
The public LibreYOLO character detector records MIT in its own metadata.
The Apache-2.0 text is preserved at `licenses/Apache-2.0.txt`.

## Public nine-grid matcher

[hshinosa/geetest-solver-nine](https://github.com/hshinosa/geetest-solver-nine)
declares MIT and author hshino in its original package metadata. Upstream has no
separate LICENSE file. Its unmodified declaration is retained as
`third_party/nine-matcher/UPSTREAM_METADATA.toml`, with provenance in NOTICE.
`GridMatcher` is a TypeScript port of the local ONNX matcher; no browser token,
site registration, external AI API or Python component is used.

The two pretrained weights are fetched from public `wulu007/gt`, fixed revision
27b45196526af62c661c87b86a90c3899b85afce, `nine/261017/`, under that model card's
Apache-2.0 declaration. Their hashes exactly match the matcher project's bundled
files. This is distinct from wulu's unavailable private nine classifier, whose
weight is not included, fetched or selected by this runtime.

## PyPasser improvements

[xHossein/PyPasser](https://github.com/xHossein/PyPasser), fixed commit
910c3def3d69e68d42d86ccba5a1b4cf105ee1ed: MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 xHossein.
Original license: `third_party/pypasser/LICENSE`.

The data-only RSA keyring, automatic risk-type detection, voice fallback strategy
and alternative Canny slide matcher reference or port its GeeTest implementation.
Downloaded JavaScript is never executed. Key changes are followed by a fresh
challenge; repeated candidate submissions against the same lot are not adopted.
No Vosk model, browser automation or Python runtime is installed.

## Public phrase lexicon

[fxsjy/jieba](https://github.com/fxsjy/jieba), fixed commit
67fa2e36e72f69d9134b8a1037b83fbb070b9775, `jieba/dict.txt`: MIT,
Copyright (c) 2013 Sun Junyi. Original license: `third_party/jieba/LICENSE`.
The unchanged dictionary is fetched as a SHA256-verified data asset. Only a unique
four-character anagram may supplement phrase ordering; verified upstream entries
take precedence and ambiguous cases defer to the original ranker. No model was trained.

## Similarity icon recognition

- [sml2h3/ddddocr](https://github.com/sml2h3/ddddocr), pinned commit
  c40f56f95412e10bcb9bd0bd24411e92f896d238: MIT. The YOLOX decoder and input
  convention were ported to TypeScript. The unchanged model matches the 1.6.1 wheel.
  Original license and notice: `third_party/ddddocr/`.
- [VeyraAgent/cf-solver-models](https://huggingface.co/VeyraAgent/cf-solver-models),
  revision 0257291b5110eeab7d13cab98907ab1347559e22: model card declares MIT for
  the unchanged embedding weight. Linked project license: `third_party/cf-solver/`.
  Its separate detector was researched but not adopted; its AGPL metadata is not
  relabeled MIT.
- [zscmmm/yzm_captcha](https://github.com/zscmmm/yzm_captcha): MIT code,
  Copyright (c) 2024 caisxg. The candidate preprocessing and matching port is
  confined to `scripts/benchmarks/candidates/`; the Apache-2.0 model-card weight
  is in that research catalog, not the production model download list.
  Original license and notice: `third_party/yzm-captcha/`.
- [LeapYa/geetest-captcha-solver](https://github.com/LeapYa/geetest-captcha-solver)
  was consulted for its published contour-matching approach. No source or weights
  were copied: it has no standalone permissive license. The benchmark's standard
  chamfer implementation was written independently and is not a default solver.

All selected weights remain unchanged. No training, Python runtime or unlicensed
copy of the research-only detector/classifier is shipped.

## Runtime libraries

Package-manager distributions retain their own notices. Direct dependencies
include ONNX Runtime (MIT), sharp (Apache-2.0), OpenCV.js (Apache-2.0),
resvg-js (MPL-2.0), sm-crypto (MIT), fft.js (MIT), fflate (MIT),
fast-xml-parser (MIT), and mpg123-decoder (MIT JavaScript wrapper; its underlying
compiled decoder retains its separate upstream notices). Native libraries and
WASM artifacts remain unmodified inside the installed package distributions.

Model comparison reports do not grant redistribution rights for research-only
candidates. Candidates with unavailable weights, undeclared preprocessing or
unclear model licenses are identified separately and not silently promoted to
production defaults.

